      "id": "cancellation",
      "what": "the cancellation rule",
      "source": "Differential Equations for Engineers, A.2 Matrix algebra",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "assumes": [
            {
              "text": "$\\kA$ is invertible: its inverse $\\kAinv$ exists."
            },
            {
              "tex": "\\kAinv\\kA = \\kI",
              "src": "A.2, Inverse"
            },
            {
              "tex": "\\kA(\\kB\\kC) = (\\kA\\kB)\\kC",
              "src": "A.2, Some rules of matrix algebra"
            },
            {
              "tex": "\\kI\\kA = \\kA",
              "src": "A.2, Some rules of matrix algebra"
            }
          ],
          "then": {
            "tex": "\\mk{a1}{\\kA}\\mk{b}{\\kB} = \\mk{a2}{\\kA}\\mk{c}{\\kC}"
          },
          "steps": [
            {
              "tex": "\\mk{i1}{\\kAinv}\\mk{a1}{\\kA}\\mk{b}{\\kB} = \\mk{i2}{\\kAinv}\\mk{a2}{\\kA}\\mk{c}{\\kC}",
              "uses": [
                0
              ],
              "cap": "Multiply both sides by $\\kAinv$, and on the same side, the left: matrices do not commute, so $\\kAinv\\kA\\kB$ and $\\kA\\kB\\kAinv$ need not be equal."
            },
            {
              "tex": "\\mk{e1}{\\kI}\\mk{b}{\\kB} = \\mk{e2}{\\kI}\\mk{c}{\\kC}",
              "uses": [
                1,
                2
              ],
              "cap": "By the associative law $\\kAinv\\kA\\kB = (\\kAinv\\kA)\\kB$, and $\\kAinv\\kA = \\kI$.",
