  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "e1",
      "source_id": "A.2.1",
      "source_number": "A.2.1",
      "kind": "exercise",
      "bloom": "Apply",
      "place": {
        "at": "end"
      },
      "cite": "entrywise",
      "prompt": "<p>Add the following matrices</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>$\\begin{bmatrix} -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 8 & -1 \\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix} 3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 5 \\end{bmatrix}$</li><li>$\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & -8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}$</li></ol>",
      "answer": {
        "type": "open",
        "generated_by": "ai",
        "solution": "a) $\\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 13 & 11 & 4 \\end{bmatrix}$ b) $\\begin{bmatrix} 3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 1 & 2 \\end{bmatrix}$. The two matrices of each part are of the same size, so we add them element-wise: each entry of the sum is the sum of the entries in the same place. In a) the first row is $-1+3,\\ 2+2,\\ 2+3 = 2,\\ 4,\\ 5$ and the second $5+8,\\ 8+3,\\ -1+5 = 13,\\ 11,\\ 4$. In b) the rows are $1+2,\\ 2-8,\\ 4-3 = 3,\\ -6,\\ 1$, then $2+3,\\ 3+1,\\ 1+0 = 5,\\ 4,\\ 1$, then $0+6,\\ 5-4,\\ 1+1 = 6,\\ 1,\\ 2$."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e2",
      "source_id": "A.2.2",
      "source_number": "A.2.2",
      "kind": "exercise",
      "bloom": "Apply",
      "place": {
        "at": "end"
      },
      "cite": "scalar-entrywise",
      "prompt": "<p>Compute</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>$3\\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\end{bmatrix} + 6 \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\end{bmatrix}$</li><li>$2\\begin{bmatrix} -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\end{bmatrix} - 3 \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 \\end{bmatrix}$</li></ol>",
      "answer": {
        "type": "open",
        "generated_by": "ai",
        "solution": "a) $\\begin{bmatrix} 6 & 39 \\\\ -12 & 36 \\end{bmatrix}$ b) $\\begin{bmatrix} -12 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -2 \\end{bmatrix}$. Scaling a matrix by a scalar scales every entry, and then the two matrices are added (or subtracted) element-wise. In a) $3\\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 6 \\end{bmatrix}$ and $6\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 6 & 30 \\\\ -6 & 30 \\end{bmatrix}$, whose sum is $\\begin{bmatrix} 6 & 39 \\\\ -12 & 36 \\end{bmatrix}$. In b) $2\\begin{bmatrix} -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} -6 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 \\end{bmatrix}$ and $3\\begin{bmatrix} 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 6 & -3 \\\\ 9 & 6 \\end{bmatrix}$, whose difference is $\\begin{bmatrix} -12 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -2 \\end{bmatrix}$."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e3",
      "source_id": "A.2.3",
      "source_number": "A.2.3",
      "kind": "exercise",
      "bloom": "Apply",
      "place": {
        "at": "end"
      },
      "cite": "matrix-product",
      "prompt": "<p>Multiply the following matrices</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>$\\begin{bmatrix} -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 8 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 3 & -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 2 & -3 \\end{bmatrix}$</li><li>$\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}$</li><li>$\\begin{bmatrix} 4 & 1 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 6 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 \\end{bmatrix}$</li><li>$\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 \\end{bmatrix}$</li></ol>",
      "answer": {
        "type": "open",
        "generated_by": "ai",
        "solution": "a) $\\begin{bmatrix} 13 & 7 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 17 & 0 & 11 & 0 \\\\ 79 & 19 & 31 & -19 \\end{bmatrix}$ b) $\\begin{bmatrix} 7 & 4 & 16 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 10 & 9 & 20 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 10 & 7 \\end{bmatrix}$ c) $\\begin{bmatrix} 42 & 70 \\\\ 31 & 62 \\\\ 32 & 62 \\end{bmatrix}$ d) $\\begin{bmatrix} 27 & 18 \\\\ 11 & 4 \\end{bmatrix}$. In each part the middle sizes match ($[3 \\times 2][2 \\times 4] = [3 \\times 4]$, $[3 \\times 3][3 \\times 4] = [3 \\times 4]$, $[3 \\times 4][4 \\times 2] = [3 \\times 2]$, $[2 \\times 3][3 \\times 2] = [2 \\times 2]$), and the $ij^{\\text{th}}$ entry of the product is the dot product $\\operatorname{row}_i \\cdot \\operatorname{column}_j$. For example, the top left entry of a) is $(-1)(3) + (2)(8) = 13$, of b) $(1)(2) + (2)(1) + (3)(1) = 7$, of c) $(4)(2) + (1)(1) + (6)(3) + (3)(5) = 42$, and of d) $(1)(2) + (1)(1) + (4)(6) = 27$; every other entry is found the same way."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e4",
      "source_id": "A.2.4",
      "source_number": "A.2.4",
      "kind": "exercise",
      "bloom": "Apply",
      "place": {
        "at": "end"
      },
      "cite": "inverse-2x2",
      "prompt": "<p>Compute the inverse of the given matrices</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>$\\begin{bmatrix} -3 \\end{bmatrix}$</li><li>$\\begin{bmatrix} 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}$</li><li>$\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\end{bmatrix}$</li><li>$\\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{bmatrix}$</li></ol>",
      "answer": {
        "type": "open",
        "generated_by": "ai",
        "solution": "a) $\\begin{bmatrix} -1/3 \\end{bmatrix}$ b) $\\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}$ c) $\\begin{bmatrix} -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\end{bmatrix}$ d) $\\begin{bmatrix} 2/3 & -1/3 \\\\ -1/6 & 1/3 \\end{bmatrix}$. For a $1 \\times 1$ matrix $[a]$ the inverse is $[1/a]$, so a) is $[-1/3]$. For the $2 \\times 2$ matrices use $\\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{smallmatrix} \\right]^{-1} = \\frac{1}{ad-bc} \\left[ \\begin{smallmatrix} d & -b \\\\ -c & a \\end{smallmatrix} \\right]$: in b) $ad - bc = 0 - (-1)(1) = 1$, giving $\\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}$; in c) $ad - bc = 3 - 4 = -1$, giving $-\\begin{bmatrix} 3 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}$; in d) $ad - bc = 8 - 2 = 6$, giving $\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix} 4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{bmatrix}$. Each determinant is nonzero, so each matrix is invertible, and multiplying each answer by its matrix gives $\\kI$."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e5",
      "source_id": "A.2.5",
      "source_number": "A.2.5",
      "kind": "exercise",
      "bloom": "Apply",
      "place": {
        "at": "end"
